{"chunk_id": "1f48f69a1ea2", "text": "This section moves the diplomacy and alliances that will shape the coming Kurukshetra war. Drupada sends a learned Brahmana priest to Hastinapura to speak righteously before Dhritarashtra and subtly weaken the loyalty of key Kaurava elders by reminding them of justice and the suffering endured by the Pandavas. Meanwhile both sides rush to gather allies. Arjuna travels to Dwaraka to seek Krishna\u2019s support, but Duryodhana arrives as well. When Krishna awakens, he offers a choice: his vast Narayana army on one side, or himself alone on the other, unarmed and vowed not to fight. Arjuna chooses Krishna; Duryodhana gladly takes the army. Balarama then refuses to support either side, declaring neutrality. The episode highlights strategy, moral positioning, and the decisive importance of Krishna\u2019s presence rather than mere military strength.\nArjuna and Duryodhana seek Krishna\u2019s support for the coming war; Arjuna chooses Krishna himself while Duryodhana takes Krishna\u2019s vast Narayana army.\nThemes: strategic diplomacy, choice between power and wisdom, prelude to Kurukshetra war, loyalty and neutrality, divine presence in politics", "vector": [0.0026923755649477243, -0.019328493624925613, -0.00241100718267262, 0.003497729543596506, -0.008336592465639114, 0.03534122183918953, -0.015864461660385132, -0.0032820699270814657, -0.01490747183561325, -0.0239516980946064, 0.02051462233066559, 0.005566714331507683, -0.004259277600795031, 0.014489631168544292, -0.01132213044911623, -0.00019523092487361282, 0.0359073281288147, -0.018816301599144936, 0.041676223278045654, -0.01798062212765217, -0.012541955336928368, -0.029302751645445824, 0.000529461249243468, 0.02618916518986225, -0.0025323156733065844, 0.03736303001642227, 0.016471004113554955, -0.027119198814034462, 0.008754433132708073, -0.019935036078095436, -0.007211118936538696, 0.003568492829799652, 0.0053611635230481625, -0.00048439172678627074, -0.015567929483950138, -0.0